commit_template_hash: 686bd6f6d3f60a9716f8ca85195b61c4852e2e6d8a91cf7a01fc867d6252a9af
intent: Fix a genuine nool 7.0.0 bug affecting nool_try's release calls: nool announce release --all --agent-id <id>'s --help says it releases 'every active lease you own' but verified via direct repro (two leases under distinct agent ids, release --all --agent-id <one>) that --agent-id does NOT filter -- --all releases EVERY active lease in the coordination store regardless of owner. This is what produced the N=10/v3 'Coordination conflict' scatter across unrelated ticket pairs in two consecutive reruns (49-50/60), not corpus contention or a leak: any ticket finishing (success OR rejection) was wiping out every OTHER concurrently in-flight ticket's admission lease, opening a window for a newly-admitted ticket to legitimately (from the confused gate's view) touch files another ticket still held. nool_gated/nool_fleet were never exposed to this because their own release calls already use the specific announcement ID when available (the pre-existing, unmodified pattern), and nool_fleet's own gate is advisory-only anyway. Fixed both of nool_try's release sites (_discard_and_release, and integrate_try's post-promote release) to look up propose's own lease by matching our unique --intent string via announce status, then release that ONE lease by its specific ID -- verified with a direct repro: ticket B's admission lease now survives ticket A's successful promote+release. The confounded 49/60 and 50/60 reruns were never landed and are discarded
knot_id: 88e1d4f3da2fb14076e20a719a560dcdd3b410d1cea92b34779b1312825f2b0c
